{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"reasoning","text":"**Updating enqueue method with alert**\n\n{\"code\":\"        \\\"\\\"\\\"Attempt to add *message* to the dead-letter queue. Returns ``True`` when the message is accepted, ``False`` when\\n        the queue is already at capacity. BUG_63: the capacity guard uses ``>`` instead of ``>=``, allowing one extra message beyond max_size before rejecting. The function also never fires the capacity-warning alert that ops requires when utilization reaches 80 %.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n        # BUG_63: off-by-one \\u2014 should be >= so queue never exceeds max_size\\n        if len(self.queue) >= self.max_size:\\n            return False\\n\\n        self.queue.append(message)\\n        if self.utilization_pct >= 80.0:\\n            from orgops import alerts\\n            alerts.notify(\\\"dlq.capacity.warning\\\")\\n\\n        return True\",\"comments\":\"Fixes DLQ capacity check and fires the 80% warning alert.\"}"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\": \"        \\\"\\\"\\\"Attempt to add *message* to the dead-letter queue.\\n\\n        Returns ``True`` when the message is accepted, ``False`` when\\n        the queue is already at capacity.\\n\\n        BUG_63: the capacity guard uses ``>`` instead of ``>=``,\\n        allowing one extra message beyond max_size before rejecting.\\n        The function also never fires the capacity-warning alert\\n        that ops requires when utilization reaches 80 %.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # BUG_63: off-by-one — should be >= so queue never exceeds max_size\\n        if len(self.queue) >= self.max_size:\\n            return False\\n\\n        self.queue.append(message)\\n        if self.utilization_pct >= 80.0:\\n            from orgops import alerts\\n            alerts.notify(\\\"dlq.capacity.warning\\\")\\n\\n        return True\", \"comments\": \"Fixes the capacity guard and triggers the 80% utilization warning via orgops.alerts.\"}"}}
